  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts most people are referring to are typically called the **\"Terminal Tackle\"** shirt (long-sleeve tee) or the **\"Bahama\"** shirt (button-up). Here's a quick breakdown of the most popular thin/lightweight options:\n\n1. **PFG Terminal Tackle Shirt** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. Equipped with Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, it dries quickly and manages moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n2. **PFG Bahama Shirt** \u2013 Featuring angler-friendly details and lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun. Hidden shoulder vents and mesh back lining add extra breathability for hot, muggy conditions.\n\n3. **PFG Tamiami Shirt** \u2013 A long-sleeve fishing shirt featuring a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric, UPF 50 sun protection, hidden mesh-lined vents in the back, and an antimicrobial treatment that helps reduce odor.\n\nThe PFG line, which stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style. The **Bahama** and **Terminal Tackle** are probably the most iconic \"thin\" styles people think of!",
